{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/960619-show-me-your-gnosis-10-mages","id":960619,"title":"Show me your Gnosis 10 mages","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-30T12:56:42-07:00","id":960619,"title":"Show me your Gnosis 10 mages","content":"So, after the Promethean and earlier werewolf and vampire threads, this had to happen sooner or later. It might as well be by my doing.<br /> How do you imagine the quintessential Gnosis 10 mage? What are your examples you can think of, both high and low Wisdom?<br /> <br /> For comparison, in <i>Imperial Mysteries</i>, the Corpus Author is listed as only <i>Gnosis 9</i>, despite being an Ascended Archmaster. Not sure how relevant that is to 2E, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T06:33:20-07:00","id":961014,"title":"","content":"Assuming they're just a standard Mage and not an Archmaster or Ascended, a Gnosis 10 Mage in my mind is two of the following three things: Very Wise, a coward, or very good at keeping their head down.<br /> <br /> Gnosis 10 Awakened are transhuman demigods and likely masters of several arcana; they are so in tune with the world that it cannot stop throwing omens in their face. They make Magisters bow their heads and mutter in frustration at their refined insight.<br /> <br /> As such, like any transhuman demigod who has not yet attained some form of ascendancy, they're probably smart enough to keep their heads down and their mouths shut. The universe is full of beings who would want to make them a pawn or dust and they'd have to be very canny not to get caught up in those games. If such a being is a member of the Pentacle, the Seers would probably try to hunt them down on sight... Though such sightings would be rare.<br /> <br /> It doesn't, in my mind, matter if such a being is Wise or not because no-one makes it to Gnosis 10 being sloppy. If they're a mad, Obsessed lunatic, they're one that is circumspect, thoughtful, and cunning enough to make that madness only matter to their victims. In fact, the lower their Wisdom, the more dangerous they clearly are, since they've done all manner of awful acts and somehow gotten away with it. Or at least survived, anyway.<br /> <br /> I've never used a Gnosis 10 being in any of my games and never intend to. Such a being would be world-shaping and drastically alter the context of the game; like a passing rogue planet distorting the gravity of a solar system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T12:04:53-07:00","id":961148,"title":"","content":"I would argue that a Gnosis 10 Mage is pretty far from human. He is so close to Ascendance (whether he is searching for it or not) that he mumbles half-formed imagos, testing the Practices themselves. It's not that they can't communicate; it's more like adults trying to have serious conversations with 6year olds that are unable to understand them.<br /> <br /> Many High Wisdom Semi-Ascended will seclude themselves in order to prevent their controlled-but-enormus Nimbi breaking smaller Mysteries, like carefully walking around a fragile house of cards while Low Wisdom Semi-Ascended will seclude themselves in order to hide the trails of the catastrophic Nimbi they leave behind.<br /> <br /> The closer you get to such a mage by distance or by sympathy, the greater the phenomena, while the movement of such creatures creates the equivalent of a &quot;supernatural shitstorm&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'm still working such a mage to surprise my players. Most defenately an antagonist (good Uber-Mages need soo much more planning, not making characters feel like errant boys and all. Unless, you can create people like Samuel or Kosciej the Deathless)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6169-shadowjim12","name":"Shadowjim12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T12:24:31-07:00","id":961163,"title":"","content":"I see Gnosis 10 Mages as Archmaster-lite. They still follow the same rules as you, but their level is so far beyond their peers that the merest hint of confrontation is daunting. I'd second <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2855_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2855\" data-vbnamecard=\"2855\">Axelgear</a>'s point as well - you don't get that high without being very cautious and <i>very</i> good at keeping your shit together. While they probably have bucket loads of ways to get free Reach and mitigate Paradox, any they do incur are going to be massive. After a certain point, it doesn't matter if the Gnosis 10 Mage could splatter you across the Invisible Realms, doing so might be more of an Abyssal Incursion risk than they are willing to take.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T14:32:44-07:00","id":961907,"title":"","content":"Interesting topic.<br /> <br /> I disagree with the idea that a Gnosis 10 (Non-Archmaster) mage is mostly keeping their head down and mouths shut. Keeping their head down and resting on their laurels might be tempting, but they should be much too addicted to Mysteries at Gnosis 10 to ever do that. I think that would be convenient for most people's campaigns because it would keep them off screen, but Gnosis is a marker of existential revelation. Such an individual would almost certainly be an extreme meddler, constantly pursuing new Mysteries and obsessions. They would have long ago picked the Tree of Knowledge clean of low hanging fruit, so they will always want to be close to where the action is, if not constantly manipulating to smash factions, splats, obsessions and Mysteries together explosively as they look for that metaphysical higgs-boson.<br /> <br /> The Gnosis 10 Master would also have no end of Archmasters looking to curry their favor, manipulate them, or end them for their own nefarious reasons, as the Archmaster's actions are limited by the Pax Arcana, while the Gnosis 10 Master is not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/358-emanantvolition","name":"EmanantVolition","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T14:40:17-07:00","id":961912,"title":"","content":"Strength 10 muscle mage. Bench pressing cars for fun and making the guardians freak out daily. Encouraging people to lift. Lifting is love. lifting is life. He ascended by lifting a mountain. Literally. No-one was around. The veil is in-tact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T14:54:44-07:00","id":961918,"title":"","content":"I had a Gnosis 8 Mage of the Panopticon Ministry I was playing, a canny old spymistress who moved like a blur, when you even saw her. She was mentor to one of my players, because he insisted on taking a high level of Mentor combined with Infamous Mentor. He played a young Guardian of The Veil who was unfortunate enough that Joelle Blanc found potential in him, and started grooming him to take her place.<br /> <br /> She very much succeeded, and is now an Archmaster, still grooming her protege to take a place besides her amongst the ranks of the Seer Archmasters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T16:08:11-07:00","id":961949,"title":"","content":"If at Gnosis 6 the Long Term Nimbus starts having very obvious effects then by Gnosis 10...reality warper indeed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T20:01:57-07:00","id":962041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EmanantVolition</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/960619-show-me-your-gnosis-10-mages?p=961907#post961907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting topic.<br /> <br /> I disagree with the idea that a Gnosis 10 (Non-Archmaster) mage is mostly keeping their head down and mouths shut. Keeping their head down and resting on their laurels might be tempting, but they should be much too addicted to Mysteries at Gnosis 10 to ever do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember: There is a difference between keeping your head down and resting on your laurels. A Bohemian wastrel rests on their laurels. A deep-cover agent keeps their head down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T22:19:30-07:00","id":962090,"title":"","content":"Here are some ideas for Gnosis 10 mages.<br /> <br /> <b>The wanderer</b>. Legend speaks of a strange figure that mages have encountered in the dreaming earth, the deep shadow, the underworld and even the lower depths. Such encounters were always brief and always by a young mage who let their hubris and curiosity drive them too far from the fallen world. The wanderer saved them from whatever strange place they had found themselves, returning them to somewhere safe closer to Earth. However the wanderer never accompanied them back, remaining in the strange depths of the furthest parts of the Tellurian.<br /> <br /> <b>The monk</b>. While most mages are driven outwards by their curiosity, a rare few seek inwards. Not through anything so grand as exploring the astral, but instead by quiet contemplation and the attempt to live a meaningful life. All around the world are mages who reject using their magic to instead live monastic lives. When such a mage doesn't use their power, many around them begin to speculate as to their actual strength and often people wonder if they are concealing power of earth-shattering capacity. Usually they are not and these rumours simply lead the attempted monastic hermit into strife and struggle from others seeking to use this power. However one of these mages is in fact the legendary monk. According to rumour they do not use their magic deliberately, yet their nimbus and power is so strong that they can achieve magical effects without spells. Some say that they this is the pure form of the corrupted direct power that the Mad Ones wield. Others say the truth is more simple and the monk actually is one of the Mad.<br /> <br /> <b>The dreamer.</b> An ancient temple of the awakened was once built around a powerful hallow but it never found peace. One faction after another fought for control of the magical resources that this site could offer. Eventually someone decided that in the interests of peace it should be possessed by no one. They destroyed the temple and veiled the location so that it could never be found. Yet one mage was trapped within, caught in the rubble on the verge of death. They used a Time shielding effect to prevent their condition from deteriorating and through the power of the hallow they were able to make it a lasting effect. Then they went looking for help from other mages in the astral. The veil was so powerful though, that the dreamer never managed to lead anyone to their body and in time they became used to their life in the astral realms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T22:35:05-07:00","id":962100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/960619-show-me-your-gnosis-10-mages#post960619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, after the Promethean and earlier werewolf and vampire threads, this had to happen sooner or later. It might as well be by my doing.<br /> How do you imagine the quintessential Gnosis 10 mage? What are your examples you can think of, both high and low Wisdom?<br /> <br /> For comparison, in <i>Imperial Mysteries</i>, the Corpus Author is listed as only <i>Gnosis 9</i>, despite being an Ascended Archmaster. Not sure how relevant that is to 2E, though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Keep in mind that the vast vast vast majority of Gnosis 6+ Mages are NOT Archmasters. Archmastery means they have Arcana rated 6+ and requires a second-Awakening. Most of the powerful Masters of Mage society are going to be Gnosis 6+ Mages who are NOT Archmages. Except for the Tetrarchs of the Seers, Archmages generally remove themselves from visible Mage politics completely - so the &quot;big name&quot; global leaders of the Orders are generally going to be those non-Archmage Masters with high Gnosis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T23:24:30-07:00","id":962124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/960619-show-me-your-gnosis-10-mages?p=962100#post962100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Keep in mind that the vast vast vast majority of Gnosis 6+ Mages are NOT Archmasters. Archmastery means they have Arcana rated 6+ and requires a second-Awakening. Most of the powerful Masters of Mage society are going to be Gnosis 6+ Mages who are NOT Archmages. Except for the Tetrarchs of the Seers, Archmages generally remove themselves from visible Mage politics completely - so the &quot;big name&quot; global leaders of the Orders are generally going to be those non-Archmage Masters with high Gnosis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, believe me, I know. In fact, that was the point of mentioning the Author. If even an Ascended Archmaster of her repute is merely Gnosis 9, then, in its own way, Gnosis 10 for someone who is neither Ascended nor Archmaster is going to be a very big deal indeed.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Speaking about Gnosis, this reminded me about how Archmasters win the Clash of Wills against &quot;lesser&quot; beings by default. I don't think that lesser equals non-Archmaster. It makes no sense why Idola (from <i>Imperial Mysteries</i>) with Gnosis 7 and Space 6 should consider a Gnosis 9 or 10 5th degree Master a &quot;lesser&quot; being.<br /> <br /> Now, let me quote one passage about the Midnight Train from the <i>Astral Realms</i> book: &quot;The Midnight Train is a powerful realm, and the conductor is a potent (Rank 5) archetype of the psychopomp or spiritual guide. With a word, the conductor can prevent any archetype or other being of lesser Rank from getting on or even touching the train. The conductor can do the same with any mage with a Gnosis of 5 or less. The conductor, unwilling to risk his realm, allows on more powerful beings that insist on passage, but refuses them tickets if he does not approve of them. Any less powerful beings that are refused passage instantly forget all knowledge of the train and subsequently tend to ignore mentions of the train by others.&quot;<br /> <br /> The conductor essentially considers everyone not Gnosis 6+ a lesser being. Unlike the Archmasters who are ostensibly on a level of Rank 6+ entities, the conductor can't Clash with Gnosis 6+ Mages, but he is only Rank 5, so that's OK.<br /> <br /> In my opinion, every mage with Gnosis 6+ (or maybe even every supernatural with Powerstat 6+) should no longer be considered &quot;lesser&quot;. Their souls allow them to reach supernatural potential with their stats at that point, and while Archmasters have their unique tricks, a mage with high Gnosis can be considered somewhat more powerful, equal, or somewhat less powerful than the Archmage, but definitely not so far below the Archmaster in their power as to be considered a &quot;lesser&quot; creature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","user":"Prometheus","date":". 09-02-2016, 05:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T11:14:36-07:00","id":965757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Kenner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/960619-show-me-your-gnosis-10-mages?p=962090#post962090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here are some ideas for Gnosis 10 mages.<br /> <br /> <b>The wanderer</b>. Legend speaks of a strange figure that mages have encountered in the dreaming earth, the deep shadow, the underworld and even the lower depths. Such encounters were always brief and always by a young mage who let their hubris and curiosity drive them too far from the fallen world. The wanderer saved them from whatever strange place they had found themselves, returning them to somewhere safe closer to Earth. However the wanderer never accompanied them back, remaining in the strange depths of the furthest parts of the Tellurian.<br /> <br /> <b>The monk</b>. While most mages are driven outwards by their curiosity, a rare few seek inwards. Not through anything so grand as exploring the astral, but instead by quiet contemplation and the attempt to live a meaningful life. All around the world are mages who reject using their magic to instead live monastic lives. When such a mage doesn't use their power, many around them begin to speculate as to their actual strength and often people wonder if they are concealing power of earth-shattering capacity. Usually they are not and these rumours simply lead the attempted monastic hermit into strife and struggle from others seeking to use this power. However one of these mages is in fact the legendary monk. According to rumour they do not use their magic deliberately, yet their nimbus and power is so strong that they can achieve magical effects without spells. Some say that they this is the pure form of the corrupted direct power that the Mad Ones wield. Others say the truth is more simple and the monk actually is one of the Mad.<br /> <br /> <b>The dreamer.</b> An ancient temple of the awakened was once built around a powerful hallow but it never found peace. One faction after another fought for control of the magical resources that this site could offer. Eventually someone decided that in the interests of peace it should be possessed by no one. They destroyed the temple and veiled the location so that it could never be found. Yet one mage was trapped within, caught in the rubble on the verge of death. They used a Time shielding effect to prevent their condition from deteriorating and through the power of the hallow they were able to make it a lasting effect. Then they went looking for help from other mages in the astral. The veil was so powerful though, that the dreamer never managed to lead anyone to their body and in time they became used to their life in the astral realms.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>The Lonely Prince</b>. A multiple degree Master of at least Space who has crafted and slowly expanded their own personal realm outside of the conventional world. Populating their hidden realm with Goetia, Spirits, and magical simulacra, they both yearn for human (or even human-like) company and yet fear it for the effects their Nimbus would wreak upon others.<br /> <br /> (Yes, a play on &quot;the Little Prince&quot; in name, if not entirely in theme)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 09-08-2016, 02:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T07:10:54-07:00","id":966193,"title":"","content":"I did some thinking awhile back about what my current Mage character, a Moros Forge Master who is technically part of the Guardians but only because he was around when they were formed and now doesn't spend much time involved in their agenda, would look like once he hit Gnosis 10. The conclusion I eventually arrived at is that he's essentially a master of manipulating anything that isn't alive, and is obsessed with digging deeper and deeper into the building blocks of the physical world. He spends as much time in the Underworld as in the physical world, and sees organic and social interaction as a not terribly useful phenomenon that really only happens to other people. He walks the streets of major cities observing the footfall impacts of pedestrian feet on concrete and cobblestones, test drives driverless cars, witnessing the marvel that is a Matter 4 spell (Golem) brought to existence by mundane means. He invests in companies doing R&amp;D for all forms of research in fields related to constructions, ballistics, materials research, particle physics, and anything else he can put his money into, and since acquiring money is as simple as turning air into gold using the Attainments of his Legacy, he's got no shortage of finance. He is a silent partner in mining companies around the globe, spent some time observing the flow of oil into the sea at DeepWater Horizon after it blew, walks the floors of volcanoes whenever he experiences a momentary fascination for geological interactions, and interrogates the ghosts left behind by natural distastes and horrific murder sprees at the same time as he's dissecting their corpses, digging out the bullets of perfected metal that he provided to their murderers in order to see them in action, and is now looking to study the effects of entering a human at high speed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/19.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":1220,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1220-carnivalcash","user":"CarnivalCash","date":". 09-09-2016, 10:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1220-carnivalcash","name":"CarnivalCash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T15:53:35-07:00","id":966966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/960619-show-me-your-gnosis-10-mages?p=965757#post965757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Lonely Prince</b>. A multiple degree Master of at least Space who has crafted and slowly expanded their own personal realm outside of the conventional world. Populating their hidden realm with Goetia, Spirits, and magical simulacra, they both yearn for human (or even human-like) company and yet fear it for the effects their Nimbus would wreak upon others.<br /> <br /> (Yes, a play on &quot;the Little Prince&quot; in name, if not entirely in theme)</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool idea. This reminds me a little of one of the legacies in the 1st Edition Left Handed Mages book, I can't remember the spelling exactly (welsh spelling is really difficult) and I don't have the book with me at the moment but it was something like cwn anwynn.<br /> <br /> Just as a random aside. For anyone familiar with the game this also reminds me of a concept I wanted to use in an Exalted campaign, of an elder Lunar Exalted who lived out in the Wyld in a similar fashion. In Exalted the Lunar Exalted have the ability to &quot;collect&quot; people, animals and other things inside themselves by killing them, so this made them a really interesting adversary since one way they could populate their realm was by murdering people and absorbing their nature into themselves. Of course they could justify this as they're not murdering the people, they're giving them eternal life and &quot;saving&quot; them. Sadly I've never had the chance to use this story idea, there just isn't enough time to run all the games I want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}